# 15. Your "urgent reporting" language needs to be workplace-specific

This:

> "Report to EPA/authorities immediately"

appears several times. 

I wouldn't teach that as the universal response.

The current AHCLPW313 wording is explicitly:

> report urgent water quality or environmental issues **according to workplace procedures**. ([Training.gov.au][3])

So your learner should first understand:

**Stop/secure → protect people → notify supervisor/workplace → follow incident/emergency procedure → notify regulator/authority where required.**

That is much more transferable.

